# Rules vs notes (scope and hygiene)

## Boundary

- **Rules (`.mdc`):** Stable how: process, triggers, safety, invariants.
- **Skills (`SKILL.md`):** On-demand workflows the user invokes.
- **Design / facts:** What we are building. Paths and write flags live in `project-map.mdc`. The `notes/` write ban lives in `anti-hallucination-verification.mdc`.
- **Staging:** Experiment space named in that Paths table. Keep out of generation.

## When to add a rule or skill

- Only when the user asks.
- Link design and schema paths. Do not paste large tables into rules.

## Hygiene

- One concern per rule file. Under ~50 lines when possible.
- No duplication across rules or skills. Link sibling paths.
- Facts and draft designs stay in design or canonical data files; rules hold behavior only.
- Durable agent output goes in `docs/` (incl. `docs/CONTEXT.md`) per project map. New scratch or audit files only when the user asks.
- File and knowledge ids: human-readable; name for **why** (role) and **how** (use).
